WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:04.011
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1.

00:00:04.071 --> 00:00:08.382
The Adventures of Tom Sawyer by Mark Twain.

00:00:08.442 --> 00:00:11.104
Retold by Nick Ballard.

00:00:11.164 --> 00:00:14.125
Read by William DeFries.

00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:30.260
Published and Copyright, Oxford University Press, 1997.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:43.614
Chapter 1.

00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:47.787
Tom and his friends.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.760
Tom!

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.080
Tom!

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.514
Where are you?

00:00:56.574 --> 00:01:00.056
No answer.

00:01:00.116 --> 00:01:03.248
Where is that boy?

00:01:03.308 --> 00:01:08.002
When I find him, I'm going to.

00:01:08.062 --> 00:01:12.011
And Polly looked under the bed.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:18.040
Then she opened the door and looked out into the garden.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.872
Home!

00:01:20.932 --> 00:01:24.464
She heard something behind her.

00:01:24.524 --> 00:01:32.750
A small boy ran past, but Aunt Polly put out her hand and stopped him.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.011
Ah, there you are!

00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:39.804
And what's that in your pocket?

00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:43.316
Nothing, Aunt Polly.

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:45.568
Nothing.

00:01:45.628 --> 00:01:47.629
It's an apple.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:49.760
I can see it.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.430
Now listen, Tom.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.572
Those apples are not for you.

00:01:55.632 --> 00:01:57.222
And I...

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:59.713
Oh, Aunt Polly!

00:01:59.773 --> 00:02:00.774
Quick!

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.514
Look behind you!

00:02:03.574 --> 00:02:07.116
So Aunt Polly looked.

00:02:07.176 --> 00:02:12.293
And Tom was out of the house in a second.

00:02:12.352 --> 00:02:15.560
She laughed quietly.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.584
Oh, I never learn.

00:02:19.644 --> 00:02:22.246
I love that, Tom.

00:02:22.306 --> 00:02:25.298
My dead sister's child.

00:02:25.358 --> 00:02:30.382
But he isn't an easy boy for an old lady.

00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:37.428
Well, it's Saturday tomorrow, and there's no school.

00:02:37.487 --> 00:02:42.408
But it isn't going to be a holiday for Tom.

00:02:42.468 --> 00:02:45.336
Oh, no.

00:02:45.396 --> 00:02:50.768
He's going to work tomorrow.

00:02:50.828 --> 00:02:56.779
Saturday was a beautiful day.

00:02:56.839 --> 00:03:05.472
It was summer and the sun was hot and there were flowers in all the gardens.

00:03:05.532 --> 00:03:11.954
It was a day for everybody to be happy.

00:03:12.014 --> 00:03:21.902
Tom came out of his house with a brush and a big pot of white paint in his hand.

00:03:21.962 --> 00:03:25.004
He looked at the fence.

00:03:25.064 --> 00:03:31.640
It was three meters high and 30 meters long.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:38.346
He put his brush in the paint and painted some of the fence.

00:03:38.406 --> 00:03:41.174
He did it again.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:51.536
Then he stopped and looked at the fence, put down his brush and sat down.

00:03:51.596 --> 00:04:03.372
There were hours of work in front of him, and he was the unhappiest boy in the village.

00:04:03.432 --> 00:04:09.555
After ten minutes, Tom had an idea.

00:04:09.614 --> 00:04:13.726
a wonderful idea.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:19.960
He took up the brush again and began work.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:25.864
He saw his friend, Joe Harper, in the street.

00:04:25.924 --> 00:04:29.206
But he didn't look at him.

00:04:29.266 --> 00:04:33.088
Joe had an apple in his hand.

00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:38.559
He came up to Tom and looked at the fence.

00:04:38.619 --> 00:04:42.850
I am sorry, Tom.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.552
Tom said nothing.

00:04:45.612 --> 00:04:50.654
The paintbrush moved up and down.

00:04:50.713 --> 00:04:55.646
Working for your aunt, said Joe.

00:04:55.706 --> 00:04:59.098
I'm going down to the river.

00:04:59.158 --> 00:05:03.410
I'm sorry you can't come with me.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:07.176
Tom put down his brush.

00:05:07.236 --> 00:05:10.060
You call this work?"

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.721
he said.

00:05:11.781 --> 00:05:16.182
Painting of fence, said Joe.

00:05:16.242 --> 00:05:19.642
Of course it's work!

00:05:19.702 --> 00:05:25.503
Perhaps it is, and perhaps it isn't.

00:05:25.563 --> 00:05:30.434
But I like it, said Tom.

00:05:30.494 --> 00:05:34.741
I can go to the river any day.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:39.389
I can't paint a fence very often."

00:05:39.449 --> 00:05:44.542
Joe watched Tom for about five minutes.

00:05:44.602 --> 00:05:50.396
Tom painted very slowly and carefully.

00:05:50.456 --> 00:05:59.690
He often stopped, moved back from the fence, and looked at his work with a smile.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:09.953
Joe began to get very interested and said Tom, can I paint a little?

00:06:10.013 --> 00:06:13.456
Tom thought for a second.

00:06:13.516 --> 00:06:16.268
I'm sorry, Joe.

00:06:16.328 --> 00:06:22.724
You see, my aunt wants me to do it because I'm good at painting.

00:06:22.783 --> 00:06:29.028
My brother said wanted to paint too, but she said no.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:34.041
Oh, please, Tom, just a little.

00:06:34.101 --> 00:06:37.062
I'm good at painting too.

00:06:37.121 --> 00:06:42.026
Hey, do you want some of my apple?

00:06:42.085 --> 00:06:46.059
No, Joe, I can't.

00:06:46.118 --> 00:06:51.653
Okay, you can have all my apple.

00:06:51.713 --> 00:06:55.666
Tom gave Joe the brush.

00:06:55.725 --> 00:07:05.816
He did not smile, but for the first time that day, He was a very happy boy.

00:07:05.876 --> 00:07:11.451
He sat down and ate Joe's apple.

00:07:11.511 --> 00:07:21.269
More friends came to laugh at Tom, but soon they all wanted to paint too.

00:07:21.329 --> 00:07:39.244
By the afternoon, Tom had three balls, an old knife, a cat with one eye, an old blue bottle, and a lot of other exciting things.

00:07:39.304 --> 00:07:45.086
He was the richest boy in St. Petersburg.

00:07:45.146 --> 00:07:54.022
And the fence, all 30 meters of it, was a beautiful white.

00:07:54.082 --> 00:07:57.654
He went back to the house.

00:07:57.714 --> 00:08:03.184
And Polly, can I go and play now?

00:08:03.244 --> 00:08:08.054
Aunt Polly came out of the house to look.

00:08:08.114 --> 00:08:16.358
When she saw the beautiful white fence, she was very pleased.

00:08:16.417 --> 00:08:22.142
She took Tom into the house and gave him an apple.

00:08:22.202 --> 00:08:30.106
Well, you can go and play, but don't come home late.

00:08:30.166 --> 00:08:37.771
Tom quickly took a second apple and ran off.

00:08:37.832 --> 00:08:51.536
On Monday morning, Tom didn't want to go to school, but Aunt Polly got him out of bed and then out of the house.

00:08:51.596 --> 00:08:58.967
In the street near the school, he met his friend, Huckleberry Finn.

00:08:59.027 --> 00:09:02.162
Hock had no mother.

00:09:02.222 --> 00:09:06.580
and his father drank whiskey all the time.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.564
So Hock lived in the streets.

00:09:10.624 --> 00:09:13.336
He didn't go to school.

00:09:13.397 --> 00:09:19.622
He was always dirty, and he never had a new shirt.

00:09:19.682 --> 00:09:22.684
But he was happy.

00:09:22.744 --> 00:09:31.952
The mothers of St. Petersburg didn't like Hock, but Tom and his friends did.

00:09:32.012 --> 00:09:34.474
Hello, Huck.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:36.164
Said Tom.

00:09:36.224 --> 00:09:39.026
What have you got there?

00:09:39.086 --> 00:09:42.058
A dead cat.

00:09:42.118 --> 00:09:45.130
What are you gonna do with it?

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:47.240
Asked Tom.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:51.943
I'm gonna take it to the graveyard tonight.

00:09:52.003 --> 00:09:53.814
Huck said.

00:09:53.874 --> 00:09:56.926
At midnight.

00:09:56.986 --> 00:09:59.189
A dead cat.

00:09:59.249 --> 00:10:04.214
can call ghosts out of their graves.

00:10:04.274 --> 00:10:09.468
I never heard that, said Tom.

00:10:09.528 --> 00:10:11.660
Is it true?

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:17.264
Well, I don't know, said Huck.

00:10:17.324 --> 00:10:23.899
Old Mrs. Hopkins told me, come with me and see.

00:10:23.959 --> 00:10:29.036
Or are you afraid of ghosts?

00:10:29.096 --> 00:10:32.881
"'Of course not,' said Tom.

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:40.305
"'Come and meow for me at my window at eleven o'clock.'"

00:10:40.365 --> 00:10:48.769
After this, Tom was late for school, and the teacher looked at him angrily.

00:10:48.789 --> 00:10:52.801
"'Tom is Sawyer.

00:10:52.861 --> 00:10:55.402
Why are ye late again?'

00:10:55.462 --> 00:10:57.392
he said.

00:10:57.452 --> 00:11:00.628
Tom began to speak.

00:11:00.688 --> 00:11:04.004
and then stopped.

00:11:04.064 --> 00:11:08.346
There was a new girl in the school room.

00:11:08.406 --> 00:11:16.822
A beautiful girl with blue eyes and long yellow hair.

00:11:16.882 --> 00:11:22.975
Tom looked and looked.

00:11:23.035 --> 00:11:28.498
Oh, how beautiful she was.

00:11:28.558 --> 00:11:34.592
And in two seconds Tom was in love.

00:11:34.652 --> 00:11:38.135
He must sit next to her.

00:11:38.195 --> 00:11:40.957
But how?

00:11:41.017 --> 00:11:50.796
In the girl's half of the room, there was only one empty chair, and it was next to the new girl.

00:11:50.856 --> 00:11:56.960
Tom thought quickly, and then looked at the teacher.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:01.860
I stopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn.

00:12:01.921 --> 00:12:09.768
He said, the teacher was very, very angry.

00:12:09.828 --> 00:12:13.540
Boys were often late for school.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:24.502
That was bad, but talking with Huckleberry Finn was worse, much worse.

00:12:24.562 --> 00:12:40.517
The teacher took his stick, and two minutes later, Tom's trousers were very hot, and the teacher's arm was very tired.

00:12:40.577 --> 00:12:48.442
Now, Tom Sawyer, you go and sit with the girls.

00:12:48.502 --> 00:12:52.596
Some of the children laughed.

00:12:52.656 --> 00:13:02.082
Tom walked to the chair next to the new girl, sat down, and opened his book.

00:13:02.142 --> 00:13:07.314
The other children began to work again.

00:13:07.374 --> 00:13:13.448
After ten minutes, the girl looked up.

00:13:13.508 --> 00:13:18.482
There was an apple on the table in front of her.

00:13:18.542 --> 00:13:23.824
She put it back on Tom's half of the table.

00:13:23.884 --> 00:13:31.038
A minute later, the apple was in front of her again.

00:13:31.098 --> 00:13:35.459
Now it stayed.

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:44.152
Next, Tom drew a picture of a house and put it in front of her.

00:13:44.212 --> 00:13:47.742
That's nice.

00:13:47.802 --> 00:13:53.983
The girl said, now draw a man.

00:13:54.043 --> 00:13:59.056
Tom drew a man next to the house.

00:13:59.116 --> 00:14:10.680
The man was taller than the house, and he had very big hands and very long legs.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:14.570
But the girl liked him.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:17.981
Can you draw me now?

00:14:18.041 --> 00:14:20.031
She asked.

00:14:20.091 --> 00:14:25.472
Tom drew a girl next to the man.

00:14:25.532 --> 00:14:29.965
You draw beautifully.

00:14:29.985 --> 00:14:34.278
I can't draw pictures.

00:14:34.338 --> 00:14:40.834
I can teach you, said Tom, after school.

00:14:40.894 --> 00:14:43.886
Oh, please.

00:14:43.946 --> 00:14:46.528
What's your name?

00:14:46.588 --> 00:14:48.710
Tom asked.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.630
Becky.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:53.443
Becky Thatcher.

00:14:53.503 --> 00:14:59.365
Just then Tom felt a hand on his head.

00:14:59.425 --> 00:15:02.336
It was the teacher.

00:15:02.396 --> 00:15:14.478
He took Tom by the ear and moved him back to his chair in the boy's half of the room.

00:15:14.538 --> 00:15:31.462
Chapter 2 In the graveyard That night Tom went to bed at half past nine.

00:15:31.522 --> 00:15:40.386
He waited for Huck's meow, and at eleven o'clock it came.

00:15:40.445 --> 00:15:53.455
He climbed quietly out of the bedroom window, and then he and Huck walked out of the village with the dead cat.

00:15:53.515 --> 00:16:01.724
The graveyard was on a hill, about a mile from St. Petersburg.

00:16:01.784 --> 00:16:12.280
When the boys got there, they put the dead cat on a grave and sat down behind some trees.

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:16.894
They watched and waited.

00:16:16.954 --> 00:16:25.000
It was very dark and very quiet.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:30.605
Do you see that new grave there?

00:16:30.665 --> 00:16:32.936
Whispered Huck.

00:16:32.996 --> 00:16:37.158
That's Hoss Williams' grave.

00:16:37.219 --> 00:16:40.830
He died last week.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:44.282
Perhaps he can hear us.

00:16:44.342 --> 00:16:46.844
Tom whispered back.

00:16:46.904 --> 00:16:50.536
Do you think he can, Huck?

00:16:50.596 --> 00:16:52.796
I don't know.

00:16:52.856 --> 00:16:55.062
But I...

00:16:55.122 --> 00:16:57.508
Oh, Tom.

00:16:57.568 --> 00:16:59.069
What is it?

00:16:59.129 --> 00:17:00.730
Shh!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:03.042
Whisper, Tom.

00:17:03.102 --> 00:17:05.754
I can see something.

00:17:05.814 --> 00:17:07.895
Look!

00:17:07.955 --> 00:17:12.489
Huck moved near to Tom.

00:17:12.549 --> 00:17:15.250
Gross!

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:16.911
He said.

00:17:16.971 --> 00:17:19.173
Three of them.

00:17:19.234 --> 00:17:22.435
They're coming here, Tom.

00:17:22.496 --> 00:17:26.257
Oh, let's go home.

00:17:26.318 --> 00:17:29.118
They can't see us.

00:17:29.178 --> 00:17:31.158
Tom whispered.

00:17:31.218 --> 00:17:33.918
Not here.

00:17:33.979 --> 00:17:38.779
Ghost can see through trees.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:42.170
Said Huck unhappily.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:48.202
They can see through everything.

00:17:48.262 --> 00:17:55.066
The ghosts moved quietly through the graveyard.

00:17:55.126 --> 00:17:59.642
and came near to the trees.

00:17:59.702 --> 00:18:03.754
Huck and Tom watched.

00:18:03.814 --> 00:18:06.926
Very afraid.

00:18:06.986 --> 00:18:18.100
Then, after a minute, Huck said, Tom, they're not ghosts.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:21.522
That's Muff Potter.

00:18:21.582 --> 00:18:24.686
So it is.

00:18:24.746 --> 00:18:28.880
And that's engine Joe.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:34.414
And the other man is Dr. Robinson.

00:18:34.474 --> 00:18:37.867
What are they doing here?

00:18:37.927 --> 00:18:41.940
They're grave robbers, Tom.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:46.104
They're going to rob a grave.

00:18:46.164 --> 00:18:50.077
My father told me about it.

00:18:50.137 --> 00:18:55.194
The doctor wants a dead body, you see.

00:18:55.254 --> 00:19:04.496
He cuts it up because he wants to learn about, shh, said Tom.

00:19:04.556 --> 00:19:08.319
They're getting near.

00:19:08.379 --> 00:19:21.029
The three men stopped at Haas Williams' grave and engine Joe and Muff Potter began to dig.

00:19:21.089 --> 00:19:26.898
10 minutes later, the grave was open.

00:19:26.958 --> 00:19:32.666
Now, doctor, said Muff Potter.

00:19:32.726 --> 00:19:38.781
You want us to take the body to your house?

00:19:38.841 --> 00:19:43.304
That's five dollars more.

00:19:43.364 --> 00:19:48.018
No, said the doctor.

00:19:48.078 --> 00:19:51.920
I gave you the money this morning.

00:19:51.981 --> 00:19:56.244
I'm not giving you any more.

00:19:56.304 --> 00:20:04.841
Now you listen to me, doctor, said engine Joe.

00:20:04.901 --> 00:20:08.254
I want that money.

00:20:08.314 --> 00:20:14.168
Do you remember a day five years ago?

00:20:14.228 --> 00:20:20.853
I came to your house and asked for something to eat.

00:20:20.913 --> 00:20:24.906
And you gave me nothing.

00:20:24.966 --> 00:20:26.986
Nothing.

00:20:27.046 --> 00:20:31.168
So give me that money."

00:20:31.228 --> 00:20:34.690
He took the doctor's arm.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:38.634
But suddenly the doctor hit him.

00:20:38.694 --> 00:20:43.717
An engine Joe fell to the ground.

00:20:43.777 --> 00:20:47.800
Don't hit my friend.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:50.622
Cried muff potter.

00:20:50.683 --> 00:20:53.424
He jumped on the doctor.

00:20:53.484 --> 00:20:58.326
And the two men began to fight.

00:20:58.386 --> 00:21:09.000
It all happened very quickly, and the two boys watched with open mouths.

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:12.751
Engine Joe got up.

00:21:12.812 --> 00:21:21.756
He had Muff Potter's knife in his hand now, and he moved behind the doctor.

00:21:21.816 --> 00:21:26.818
Then the doctor hit Muff Potter on the head.

00:21:26.878 --> 00:21:30.593
Muff fell to the ground.

00:21:30.653 --> 00:21:40.292
And at the same moment, the knifing engine Joe's hand went into the doctor's back.

00:21:40.352 --> 00:21:51.088
The doctor fell to the ground on top of Muff Potter, and he did not move again.

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:56.372
The two boys could watch no more.

00:21:56.432 --> 00:21:59.586
Very quietly.

00:21:59.646 --> 00:22:11.204
They moved away from the trees and then ran out of the graveyard and back to the village.

00:22:11.264 --> 00:22:21.809
In Jin-jo stood by Hoss Williams' grave and looked down at the two men.

00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:30.246
Then he put the knife into Muff Potter's hand and sat down.

00:22:30.306 --> 00:22:39.264
Three, four, five minutes went by.

00:22:39.324 --> 00:22:45.769
Potter moved a little and opened his eyes.

00:22:45.829 --> 00:22:48.852
What?

00:22:48.912 --> 00:22:52.243
What happened, Joe?

00:22:52.304 --> 00:22:54.586
He asked.

00:22:54.646 --> 00:23:00.370
This is bad, Muff, said Joe.

00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:04.212
Why did you kill him?

00:23:04.272 --> 00:23:14.096
Muff looked at the doctor's dead body, then at the knife in his hand.

00:23:14.156 --> 00:23:16.617
Me?

00:23:16.678 --> 00:23:20.128
Did I kill him?

00:23:20.188 --> 00:23:28.223
His face went white, and the knife fell from his hand.

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:32.375
It's the whiskey, Joe.

00:23:32.436 --> 00:23:37.748
I never fight with knives, usually.

00:23:37.808 --> 00:23:45.582
Oh, why did I drink all that whiskey tonight?

00:23:45.642 --> 00:23:50.836
I don't remember anything.

00:23:50.896 --> 00:23:54.398
It's okay, muff.

00:23:54.458 --> 00:23:56.521
Said Joe.

00:23:56.582 --> 00:24:00.456
I'm not going to tell anyone.

00:24:00.516 --> 00:24:03.966
You get away quickly.

00:24:04.026 --> 00:24:06.127
Go on.

00:24:06.187 --> 00:24:09.298
Go now.

00:24:09.358 --> 00:24:15.758
Muff Potter got up and ran away.

00:24:15.818 --> 00:24:19.319
Joe watched him for a minute.

00:24:19.379 --> 00:24:25.549
Then he carefully put the knife next to the doctor's body.

00:24:25.610 --> 00:24:32.864
Then he too, left the graveyard.

00:24:32.924 --> 00:24:47.377
The next day, the sheriff's men found the doctor's body in the graveyard, and Muff potter's knife.

00:24:47.437 --> 00:24:54.291
That night, Muff came to the graveyard to get his knife.

00:24:54.351 --> 00:25:03.145
But the sheriff's men were there, and they took Muff to St. Petersburg's little jail.

00:25:03.206 --> 00:25:13.433
And there Muff sat for four weeks and waited for his trial.

00:25:13.493 --> 00:25:21.259
Tom and Huck could not forget that night in the graveyard.

00:25:21.319 --> 00:25:25.060
They were very unhappy.

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:29.210
and very afraid.

00:25:29.270 --> 00:25:32.572
What are we gonna do?

00:25:32.632 --> 00:25:34.574
Said Tom.

00:25:34.634 --> 00:25:37.885
Muff Potter didn't kill the doctor.

00:25:37.905 --> 00:25:41.136
Engine Joe did.

00:25:41.196 --> 00:25:42.847
We saw him.

00:25:42.867 --> 00:25:46.118
I know.

00:25:46.178 --> 00:25:48.250
Hux said.

00:25:48.310 --> 00:25:52.021
But what can we do?

00:25:52.082 --> 00:25:55.981
We can't tell anyone.

00:25:56.041 --> 00:25:59.801
I'm afraid of engine Joe.

00:25:59.861 --> 00:26:03.134
He's dangerous.

00:26:03.194 --> 00:26:06.306
And he's a killer.

00:26:06.366 --> 00:26:10.448
Do you want a knife in your back?

00:26:10.508 --> 00:26:12.950
Yes.

00:26:13.010 --> 00:26:18.334
I'm afraid of him too, Tom said.

00:26:18.394 --> 00:26:21.706
He thought for a minute.

00:26:21.766 --> 00:26:25.438
I'm sorry for my potter.

00:26:25.498 --> 00:26:28.288
But you're right, Huck.

00:26:28.348 --> 00:26:36.384
We can't tell anyone about engine Joe.

00:26:36.444 --> 00:26:53.461
Chapter 3 On Jackson's Island, the summer holidays came, and there was no school.

00:26:53.521 --> 00:27:02.603
Tom didn't want to think about muff potter and engine Joe, but it wasn't easy.

00:27:02.663 --> 00:27:20.008
At night, when he was in bed, he saw engine Joe's face in the dark, and he couldn't sleep, but he couldn't talk to anyone about it.

00:27:20.068 --> 00:27:28.748
One hot summer's day, He and Joe Harper were down by the Mississippi River.

00:27:28.808 --> 00:27:36.262
They sat and watched the boats and fished and talked.

00:27:36.322 --> 00:27:42.284
Let's get away from here, said Tom, suddenly.

00:27:42.344 --> 00:27:47.176
Let's go and do something exciting somewhere.

00:27:47.236 --> 00:27:51.016
Okay, said Joe.

00:27:51.076 --> 00:27:52.756
But what?

00:27:52.816 --> 00:27:54.764
And where?

00:27:54.824 --> 00:27:57.966
I know," Tom said.

00:27:58.026 --> 00:28:00.248
Let's run away.

00:28:00.308 --> 00:28:04.860
Let's go and live on Jackson's Island.

00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:09.922
We can sleep out under the trees.

00:28:09.982 --> 00:28:18.886
Jackson's Island was in the Mississippi, three miles south of St. Petersburg.

00:28:18.946 --> 00:28:22.362
Nobody lived there.

00:28:22.423 --> 00:28:27.750
Let's ask Huck Finn too, said Tom.

00:28:27.810 --> 00:28:32.982
But don't tell your mother or father or anyone.

00:28:33.042 --> 00:28:41.727
Go home and get some things to eat and meet me here at midnight.

00:28:41.787 --> 00:28:53.452
So that night, three boys in a small boat went down the river to Jackson's island.

00:28:53.512 --> 00:29:01.214
They had some bread and some meat, and Huck had his pipe, too.

00:29:01.274 --> 00:29:11.970
When they got there, they carried everything on to the island and made a fire under a big old tree.

00:29:12.029 --> 00:29:22.548
Then they cooked some of the meat over the fire, and oh, that meat was good.

00:29:22.608 --> 00:29:27.482
the best dinner in the world.

00:29:27.542 --> 00:29:31.523
Soon they stopped talking.

00:29:31.583 --> 00:29:37.736
Their eyes closed and they slept.

00:29:37.796 --> 00:29:48.568
The next morning Tom woke up with the sun on his head and a smile on his face.

00:29:48.628 --> 00:29:52.350
Then Hawk and Joe woke up.

00:29:52.410 --> 00:29:58.033
and the three boys ran down to the river to swim.

00:29:58.093 --> 00:30:07.698
After that they fished, and soon they had about six big fish for their breakfast.

00:30:07.759 --> 00:30:13.502
They cooked the fish on their fire and ate them all.

00:30:13.562 --> 00:30:17.414
They were very hungry.

00:30:17.474 --> 00:30:21.836
That said Joe happily.

00:30:21.896 --> 00:30:26.596
was a wonderful breakfast.

00:30:26.656 --> 00:30:39.878
After breakfast, they walked through the island, swam some more, talked, fished, and swam again.

00:30:39.938 --> 00:30:44.669
They came back to their fire in the afternoon.

00:30:44.729 --> 00:30:54.998
Suddenly, Tom looked up and said, Can you hear boats?"

00:30:55.058 --> 00:31:03.182
They listened, and then ran across the island to look down the river.

00:31:03.242 --> 00:31:08.036
There were twenty or more boats on the water.

00:31:08.096 --> 00:31:13.068
Every boat in St. Petersburg was out.

00:31:13.128 --> 00:31:16.350
What are they doing?

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:18.562
asked Joe.

00:31:18.622 --> 00:31:25.406
They're looking for a dead body, I think," said Hock.

00:31:25.466 --> 00:31:31.781
They did that last summer when Bill Turner fell in the river and drowned.

00:31:31.801 --> 00:31:36.704
"'Who's dead, do you think?"

00:31:36.764 --> 00:31:38.966
asked Joe.

00:31:39.026 --> 00:31:42.748
The boys watched the boats.

00:31:42.808 --> 00:31:45.770
Suddenly Tom cried.

00:31:45.790 --> 00:31:48.938
"'I know who's dead!"

00:31:48.998 --> 00:31:50.485
It's us.

00:31:50.545 --> 00:31:54.457
They're looking for us.

00:31:54.517 --> 00:31:59.110
This was wonderful.

00:31:59.170 --> 00:32:02.852
Tom looked at his friends.

00:32:02.912 --> 00:32:07.514
We're famous, he said.

00:32:07.574 --> 00:32:13.418
Everybody in St. Petersburg is talking about us.

00:32:13.478 --> 00:32:18.716
And they all feel sorry for us.

00:32:18.776 --> 00:32:25.214
Night came, and the boys went to sleep.

00:32:25.274 --> 00:32:29.004
But Tom did not sleep.

00:32:29.064 --> 00:32:34.986
And when morning came, he wasn't there.

00:32:35.046 --> 00:32:37.037
Huck!

00:32:37.097 --> 00:32:38.878
Where's Tom?

00:32:38.938 --> 00:32:41.348
cried Joe.

00:32:41.408 --> 00:32:43.990
I don't know.

00:32:44.050 --> 00:32:45.790
Huck began.

00:32:45.850 --> 00:32:49.206
But look!

00:32:49.266 --> 00:32:51.660
There he is.

00:32:51.721 --> 00:32:56.312
He's swimming across to the island now.

00:32:56.372 --> 00:33:00.723
Hey, Tom!

00:33:00.783 --> 00:33:07.004
At breakfast, Tom told his story.

00:33:07.065 --> 00:33:15.037
I went home last night, he said, and listened at the window.

00:33:15.097 --> 00:33:19.118
Joe, your mother was there too.

00:33:19.178 --> 00:33:25.322
And she and Aunt Polly cried and cried.

00:33:25.382 --> 00:33:30.236
I heard some very interesting things.

00:33:30.296 --> 00:33:40.414
On Sunday, there's going to be a big funeral at the church for us.

00:33:40.474 --> 00:33:47.414
And listen, I've got a wonderful idea.

00:33:47.474 --> 00:33:52.912
Hot ganjo listened and laughed.

00:33:52.972 --> 00:34:01.459
And yes, it was a wonderful idea.

00:34:01.519 --> 00:34:14.610
That night the boys cooked some more fish, and after dinner, Hot got out his pipe and began to smoke.

00:34:14.670 --> 00:34:17.512
Can we smoke too?

00:34:17.572 --> 00:34:19.275
asked Tom.

00:34:19.336 --> 00:34:22.050
I want to learn.

00:34:22.110 --> 00:34:31.448
So Huck made pipes for Tom and Joe, and the three boys sat and smoked.

00:34:31.508 --> 00:34:36.934
Hey, I like smoking, said Tom.

00:34:36.994 --> 00:34:39.376
It's easy.

00:34:39.436 --> 00:34:43.389
It's nothing, said Joe.

00:34:43.449 --> 00:34:47.655
I'm going to smoke every day.

00:34:47.716 --> 00:35:02.716
But after ten minutes, Tom and Joe got quieter and quieter, and their faces went an interesting color.

00:35:02.776 --> 00:35:09.309
I'm going for a little walk now, said Tom.

00:35:09.369 --> 00:35:16.558
He stood up carefully and walked away into the trees.

00:35:16.618 --> 00:35:22.507
Me too, said Joe, quickly.

00:35:22.567 --> 00:35:32.555
The two boys came back an hour later, but they didn't smoke their pipes again.

00:35:32.615 --> 00:35:46.054
On Sunday morning, there were no happy faces in St. Petersburg, and Polly and Joe's mother and father were in the church.

00:35:46.114 --> 00:35:49.324
and all the boys' friends.

00:35:49.384 --> 00:36:01.320
The minister said some very nice things about the three boys, and the boys' families cried and cried.

00:36:01.380 --> 00:36:12.262
Everybody cried, and little Becky Thatcher did not stop crying for one second.

00:36:12.322 --> 00:36:17.560
There was a small noise at the back of the church.

00:36:17.620 --> 00:36:21.652
But at first, nobody heard it.

00:36:21.712 --> 00:36:28.937
Then the minister looked up and suddenly stopped speaking.

00:36:28.997 --> 00:36:32.649
Everybody turned to look.

00:36:32.709 --> 00:36:42.883
Their mouths opened and stayed open and into the church.

00:36:42.943 --> 00:36:46.092
came the three dead boys.

00:36:46.152 --> 00:36:53.005
Tom first, Joe next, and then Huck.

00:36:53.066 --> 00:36:59.098
For a second, nobody moved or spoke.

00:36:59.158 --> 00:37:03.550
And then the noise began.

00:37:03.610 --> 00:37:16.578
Aunt Polly and Joe's mother ran to the boys and took them in their arms Aunt Polly cried, and laughed, and cried again.

00:37:16.598 --> 00:37:20.289
Oh, Tom!

00:37:20.349 --> 00:37:27.870
She said, you're a bad boy, but I love you.

00:37:27.931 --> 00:37:33.372
Suddenly the minister called out.

00:37:33.432 --> 00:37:37.366
Oh, happy days!

00:37:37.426 --> 00:37:42.900
Sing good people of St. Petersburg!

00:37:42.960 --> 00:37:48.694
Sing and be happy!

00:37:48.754 --> 00:37:59.440
And everybody sang and smiled and laughed for a long time.

00:37:59.500 --> 00:38:06.270
It was St. Petersburg's happiest funeral.

00:38:06.330 --> 00:38:13.790
The weeks went by, and the judge came to St. Petersburg.

00:38:13.850 --> 00:38:22.973
On the day before Muff Potter's trial, Huck and Tom met in the street near Tom's house.

00:38:23.033 --> 00:38:26.754
Huck was unhappy.

00:38:26.814 --> 00:38:32.196
Tom, you didn't tell anyone about.

00:38:32.256 --> 00:38:34.636
You know.

00:38:34.696 --> 00:38:37.068
No, I didn't.

00:38:37.128 --> 00:38:41.090
But Huck What about Muff?

00:38:41.150 --> 00:38:44.832
People are saying he's the killer.

00:38:44.892 --> 00:38:48.744
And he's going to die.

00:38:48.804 --> 00:38:57.069
But we can't tell anyone about engine Joe, said Hock.

00:38:57.130 --> 00:39:00.472
I don't want to die too.

00:39:00.533 --> 00:39:03.164
Do you?

00:39:03.224 --> 00:39:05.505
No.

00:39:05.566 --> 00:39:08.790
Tom didn't want to die.

00:39:08.850 --> 00:39:14.807
But he couldn't forget Muff Potter's face in the jail.

00:39:14.867 --> 00:39:21.253
Old, tired, and unhappy.

00:39:21.313 --> 00:39:26.157
An engine Joe was a free man.

00:39:26.217 --> 00:39:30.140
It wasn't right.

00:39:30.200 --> 00:39:38.304
That night, Tom came home late and very excited.

00:39:38.364 --> 00:39:44.014
He could not sleep for two or three hours.

00:39:44.074 --> 00:39:51.567
The next morning, all the village was at Muff Potter's trial.

00:39:51.628 --> 00:39:55.880
Engine Joe was there too.

00:39:55.940 --> 00:39:58.961
Muff waited.

00:39:59.021 --> 00:40:04.484
A tired old man with a dirty face.

00:40:04.544 --> 00:40:09.044
The judge began the trial.

00:40:09.104 --> 00:40:19.780
questions, questions, questions, answers, answers, answers.

00:40:19.841 --> 00:40:26.425
And the answers were all bad for Muff Potter.

00:40:26.485 --> 00:40:35.532
Yes, I found the knife in the graveyard next to Dr. Robinson's body.

00:40:35.592 --> 00:40:40.346
Yes, that's Muff Potter's knife.

00:40:40.406 --> 00:40:44.339
He always carries it.

00:40:44.399 --> 00:40:51.402
Yes, I saw Muff Potter in the village that afternoon.

00:40:51.462 --> 00:40:56.135
He had the knife with him then.

00:40:56.195 --> 00:41:03.719
Muff Potter began to look more and more unhappy.

00:41:03.780 --> 00:41:11.480
Then the judge said, called Thomas Sawyer.

00:41:11.540 --> 00:41:16.040
St. Petersburg sat up.

00:41:16.100 --> 00:41:20.574
What did young Tom Sawyer know?

00:41:20.634 --> 00:41:26.459
Everybody looked at him and waited.

00:41:26.519 --> 00:41:38.038
Thomas Sawyer, where were you on the 17th of June at the hour of midnight?

00:41:38.098 --> 00:41:42.658
In the graveyard, Why?

00:41:42.678 --> 00:41:54.497
I went there to see ghosts with a dead cat.

00:41:54.557 --> 00:42:02.013
St. Petersburg laughed, and the judge looked angry.

00:42:02.073 --> 00:42:08.598
And where were you in the graveyard, Thomas?

00:42:08.658 --> 00:42:14.962
behind the trees near Haas William's grave.

00:42:15.022 --> 00:42:21.106
Engine Joe's face suddenly went white.

00:42:21.166 --> 00:42:30.213
Now, my boy, said the judge, tell us your story.

00:42:30.273 --> 00:42:35.368
And so Tom told his story.

00:42:35.428 --> 00:42:43.748
and St. Petersburg sat and listened to him with open mouths.

00:42:43.808 --> 00:42:48.632
And then, Muff Potter fell.

00:42:48.692 --> 00:42:53.406
An engine Joe jumped with the knife and...

00:42:53.466 --> 00:42:55.388
Crash!

00:42:55.448 --> 00:43:04.901
Engine Joe jumped through the window and was out and away in a second.

00:43:04.961 --> 00:43:11.542
St. Petersburg loved Tom for a week.

00:43:11.602 --> 00:43:15.794
But Tom was not happy.

00:43:15.854 --> 00:43:19.756
Engine Joe was not in jail.

00:43:19.816 --> 00:43:24.330
And he was a dangerous man.

00:43:24.390 --> 00:43:29.363
Tom slept badly for weeks.

00:43:29.423 --> 00:43:34.696
The slow summer days went by.

00:43:34.756 --> 00:43:45.664
Engine Joe did not come back to St. Petersburg, and Tom began to forget.

00:43:45.724 --> 00:44:03.394
Chapter 4 Treasure There is a time in every boy's life when he wants to go and dig for treasure.

00:44:03.454 --> 00:44:07.834
And that time came for Tom.

00:44:07.894 --> 00:44:14.806
So, one hot summer's day, he went to find Huck.

00:44:14.866 --> 00:44:18.716
Huck liked the idea of treasure.

00:44:18.776 --> 00:44:22.018
Where are we going to dig?

00:44:22.078 --> 00:44:23.988
He asked.

00:44:24.048 --> 00:44:28.269
An old dead tree is best.

00:44:28.329 --> 00:44:33.243
Who puts the treasure under old trees?

00:44:33.303 --> 00:44:37.598
Robbers," said Tom.

00:44:37.658 --> 00:44:45.404
And then they go away, or they forget to come back for the treasure.

00:44:45.464 --> 00:44:51.798
There's a dead tree on Cardiff Hill, said Huck.

00:44:51.858 --> 00:44:54.260
Let's go there.

00:44:54.320 --> 00:44:58.804
I've got an old pick and shovel.

00:44:58.864 --> 00:45:03.712
It was three miles to the old tree.

00:45:03.772 --> 00:45:08.949
and the boys arrived tired and hot.

00:45:09.009 --> 00:45:17.210
They dug for an hour or two, but they didn't find any treasure.

00:45:17.270 --> 00:45:26.222
Then they stopped, and Tom looked down at an old house at the foot of the hill.

00:45:26.282 --> 00:45:28.623
Hey, look!

00:45:28.683 --> 00:45:33.710
He said, nobody lives in that old house.

00:45:33.770 --> 00:45:36.296
Let's go there.

00:45:36.357 --> 00:45:41.868
Old houses are always good for treasure.

00:45:41.928 --> 00:45:48.310
Good for ghosts, too, said Huck.

00:45:48.370 --> 00:45:58.472
They took the pick and shovel with them, went down the hill and into the old house.

00:45:58.532 --> 00:46:03.319
They looked in all the rooms downstairs.

00:46:03.379 --> 00:46:06.446
and then went upstairs.

00:46:06.506 --> 00:46:12.509
But there was no treasure and no ghosts.

00:46:12.570 --> 00:46:17.022
Then they heard a noise.

00:46:17.082 --> 00:46:21.644
Shh, said Tom suddenly.

00:46:21.705 --> 00:46:24.176
What's that?

00:46:24.236 --> 00:46:29.408
Ghosts, whispered Huck.

00:46:29.469 --> 00:46:33.011
There were holes in the floor.

00:46:33.071 --> 00:46:39.265
And through them, the boys could see into the rooms downstairs.

00:46:39.325 --> 00:46:41.526
No.

00:46:41.587 --> 00:46:43.668
Tom whispered.

00:46:43.728 --> 00:46:46.338
It's two men.

00:46:46.399 --> 00:46:50.120
One is the old Spaniard.

00:46:50.181 --> 00:46:54.514
He came to live in the village last week.

00:46:54.574 --> 00:46:57.876
I don't know the other man.

00:46:57.936 --> 00:46:59.576
Shh.

00:46:59.636 --> 00:47:02.954
Let's listen to them.

00:47:03.014 --> 00:47:08.402
The two men sat down on the floor.

00:47:08.462 --> 00:47:15.394
The Spaniard had a green hat and long white hair.

00:47:15.455 --> 00:47:20.756
The other man was small and dark.

00:47:20.817 --> 00:47:29.052
He took out a bag and began to open it.

00:47:29.112 --> 00:47:35.756
He took off his green hat.

00:47:35.816 --> 00:47:42.317
And then, he took off his long white hair.

00:47:42.378 --> 00:47:45.038
Tom!

00:47:45.098 --> 00:47:48.050
Huck whispered upstairs.

00:47:48.110 --> 00:47:53.040
That's engine Joe!

00:47:53.100 --> 00:48:00.014
We took $650 when we robbed that house.

00:48:00.074 --> 00:48:04.887
Set the second man.

00:48:04.947 --> 00:48:09.140
He took some money out of the bag.

00:48:09.200 --> 00:48:14.494
We can take $50 with us now.

00:48:14.554 --> 00:48:20.208
What are we going to do with the 600?

00:48:20.268 --> 00:48:23.541
Leave it here.

00:48:23.601 --> 00:48:26.603
Set engine Joe.

00:48:26.663 --> 00:48:32.128
We can come back and get it next week.

00:48:32.188 --> 00:48:37.162
Here, give me the bag."

00:48:37.222 --> 00:48:50.685
He walked across the room to the fireplace, moved two big stones from the floor, and began to dig with his knife.

00:48:50.745 --> 00:48:58.378
Upstairs, the two boys watched excitedly.

00:48:58.438 --> 00:49:06.568
Six hundred dollars of wonderful treasure.

00:49:06.628 --> 00:49:10.938
Engine Joe stopped digging.

00:49:10.998 --> 00:49:13.170
Hello.

00:49:13.230 --> 00:49:14.990
What's this?

00:49:15.050 --> 00:49:16.890
He said.

00:49:16.951 --> 00:49:20.202
There's something here.

00:49:20.262 --> 00:49:23.794
It's an old box.

00:49:23.854 --> 00:49:30.667
The two men got the box out and opened it.

00:49:30.727 --> 00:49:37.110
It's money," said Injun Joe's friend.

00:49:37.170 --> 00:49:42.482
Injun Joe put his hand into the box.

00:49:42.542 --> 00:49:49.945
There are thousands of dollars here, he said.

00:49:50.005 --> 00:49:57.188
And the two men looked at the money with happy smiles.

00:49:57.248 --> 00:50:00.197
But who?

00:50:00.258 --> 00:50:03.958
began Engine Joe's friend.

00:50:04.018 --> 00:50:08.722
Don't ask, Engine Joe said.

00:50:08.782 --> 00:50:13.024
It's our money now.

00:50:13.084 --> 00:50:19.298
We can't take it with us today, said his friend.

00:50:19.359 --> 00:50:22.040
What can we do with it?

00:50:22.100 --> 00:50:26.002
Put it back under the floor?

00:50:26.062 --> 00:50:31.165
Yes, said Engine Joe.

00:50:31.225 --> 00:50:35.396
Happy faces upstairs.

00:50:35.456 --> 00:50:38.166
No.

00:50:38.226 --> 00:50:43.628
Very unhappy faces upstairs.

00:50:43.688 --> 00:50:47.429
Let's put it under the cross.

00:50:47.489 --> 00:50:50.320
Nobody goes there.

00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:55.222
We can take it there tonight.

00:50:55.282 --> 00:51:02.564
When night came, the two men carried all the money away.

00:51:02.624 --> 00:51:09.746
The boys did not go after them, because they were afraid of engine Joe.

00:51:09.806 --> 00:51:18.728
But they wanted very much to find that cross.

00:51:18.788 --> 00:51:27.801
For a week the two boys thought and thought about the treasure.

00:51:27.861 --> 00:51:37.248
It was under the cross Where was the cross?

00:51:37.308 --> 00:51:54.430
In St. Petersburg, the boys watched the Spaniard carefully, but they didn't see a cross, and they didn't find the treasure.

00:51:54.490 --> 00:52:09.972
Chapter 5 In the Cave The next Saturday was Becky Thatcher's birthday.

00:52:10.033 --> 00:52:15.534
And all Becky's friends were very excited.

00:52:15.594 --> 00:52:20.376
It's going to be a wonderful day.

00:52:20.437 --> 00:52:23.088
Becky told Tom.

00:52:23.148 --> 00:52:27.219
We're going to have a picnic by the river.

00:52:27.279 --> 00:52:33.846
And after that, we can visit McDougall's cave.

00:52:33.906 --> 00:52:44.900
So in the morning, a big boat took Becky, Tom, and all their friends down the river.

00:52:44.960 --> 00:52:54.528
There were some older children on the boat too, but all the mothers and fathers stayed at home.

00:52:54.588 --> 00:52:59.292
Picnics are better without them.

00:52:59.352 --> 00:53:06.114
And it was a very happy, noisy picnic.

00:53:06.174 --> 00:53:17.098
After the picnic, the children took out their candles and ran up the hill to the cave.

00:53:17.158 --> 00:53:25.662
The mouth of the cave was dark, and some of the children were afraid at first.

00:53:25.722 --> 00:53:34.548
But caves are exciting, so in the end everybody went in.

00:53:34.608 --> 00:53:45.636
McDougall's cave was very, very big, with hundreds of tunnels and rooms.

00:53:45.696 --> 00:53:53.562
The tunnels went up, down, and into the hill for miles.

00:53:53.622 --> 00:53:59.347
You could walk for days in McDougall's cave.

00:53:59.407 --> 00:54:03.328
Nobody knew all the cave.

00:54:03.388 --> 00:54:08.298
but many people knew the tunnels near the door.

00:54:08.358 --> 00:54:13.942
You could play all day in these tunnels.

00:54:14.002 --> 00:54:19.216
Tom, of course, knew them well.

00:54:19.276 --> 00:54:42.786
For hours, the children walked and ran through the cave, up and down the tunnels, in and out of the rooms, In the evening they came out, and walked down the hill to the boat, tired but happy.

00:54:42.846 --> 00:54:49.620
When the boat arrived back in St. Petersburg, it was dark.

00:54:49.680 --> 00:54:56.464
Huck Finn saw the boat, but he did not know about the picnic.

00:54:56.524 --> 00:55:01.134
He did not go to birthday picnics, of course.

00:55:01.194 --> 00:55:06.771
because the mothers of St. Petersburg did not like him.

00:55:06.831 --> 00:55:16.363
But tonight, Hock was only interested in treasure, engine Joe's treasure.

00:55:16.423 --> 00:55:27.036
Engine Joe was in an old building by the river, and Hock waited in the street near the building.

00:55:27.096 --> 00:55:35.949
Perhaps he thought Engine Joe's cross isn't there.

00:55:36.009 --> 00:55:39.350
And the box of money.

00:55:39.410 --> 00:55:43.780
I must wait and watch.

00:55:43.841 --> 00:55:49.192
I can tell Tom about it tomorrow.

00:55:49.252 --> 00:55:54.583
But Engine Joe didn't come out.

00:55:54.643 --> 00:55:58.982
At midnight, it began to rain.

00:55:59.042 --> 00:56:05.121
and Hock waited all night in the cold street.

00:56:05.182 --> 00:56:12.583
In the morning he could not move, and he could not speak.

00:56:12.643 --> 00:56:22.216
He felt cold, then hot, then cold, then hot again.

00:56:22.276 --> 00:56:29.742
Mrs. Douglas, a woman from the church, found him in the street.

00:56:29.802 --> 00:56:35.478
She took him to her home and put him to bed.

00:56:35.538 --> 00:56:40.860
And there he stayed for two weeks.

00:56:40.920 --> 00:56:44.260
He was very ill.

00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:49.822
And so he did not hear about Tom and Becky.

00:56:49.882 --> 00:56:58.281
But on Sunday morning, all Saint Petersburg knew about Tom and Becky.

00:56:58.341 --> 00:57:04.588
because they were not on the boat when it came back to the village.

00:57:04.648 --> 00:57:07.728
Where were they?

00:57:07.788 --> 00:57:11.339
Were they lost in the cave?

00:57:11.400 --> 00:57:18.400
And were they alive or dead?

00:57:18.460 --> 00:57:26.232
At first, Tom and Becky played with their friends in the cave.

00:57:26.292 --> 00:57:33.446
Then Tom wanted to go down a new tunnel, and Becky went with him.

00:57:33.506 --> 00:57:42.089
They walked and talked and went into a second tunnel, then a third.

00:57:42.149 --> 00:57:48.492
Sometimes Tom put a mark with candle smoke on the tunnel wall.

00:57:48.552 --> 00:57:53.444
He wanted to find the mouth of the cave again.

00:57:53.504 --> 00:58:07.338
Then they came out of the tunnels There were hundreds of bats in this room, and the candles woke them up.

00:58:07.399 --> 00:58:15.844
Tom took Becky's hand and they ran into the nearest tunnel with the bats behind them.

00:58:15.904 --> 00:58:21.888
But one bat hit Becky's candle and it went out.

00:58:21.948 --> 00:58:31.414
The children ran and ran through the tunnels, and at last they got away from the bats.

00:58:31.474 --> 00:58:35.257
They stopped and sat down.

00:58:35.317 --> 00:58:42.562
Suddenly, it was very, very quiet.

00:58:42.622 --> 00:58:47.024
Where are we now, Tom?

00:58:47.084 --> 00:58:51.397
Becky whispered, afraid.

00:58:51.457 --> 00:58:55.100
I don't know, said Tom.

00:58:55.160 --> 00:58:57.962
I think it's time to go back.

00:58:58.022 --> 00:59:03.088
But we can't go through that big room because of the bats.

00:59:03.149 --> 00:59:06.945
Let's go down this tunnel.

00:59:07.005 --> 00:59:16.591
They went down one tunnel, then a second, a third, a fourth.

00:59:16.651 --> 00:59:21.514
Then they wanted to find the big room with the bats again.

00:59:21.574 --> 00:59:24.246
But they couldn't.

00:59:24.306 --> 00:59:28.088
Becky began to cry.

00:59:28.149 --> 00:59:32.536
Tom, we can't get out.

00:59:32.596 --> 00:59:35.381
We're lost, Tom!

00:59:35.441 --> 00:59:38.772
We're lost!

00:59:38.832 --> 00:59:43.764
They walked and walked.

00:59:43.824 --> 00:59:48.716
When they were tired, they sat down.

00:59:48.776 --> 00:59:53.348
Then they got up and walked again.

00:59:53.408 --> 00:59:56.659
Time went by.

00:59:56.720 --> 01:00:01.042
Was it day or night?

01:00:01.102 --> 01:00:04.470
They didn't know.

01:00:04.530 --> 01:00:09.428
Then Tom wanted to find water.

01:00:09.488 --> 01:00:16.729
They had nothing to eat, and they must have something to drink.

01:00:16.789 --> 01:00:24.540
They found a very small river, and sat down next to it.

01:00:24.600 --> 01:00:38.122
Becky, said Tom, we must stay here, near this river, This is our last candle and...

01:00:38.182 --> 01:00:41.213
He did not finish.

01:00:41.273 --> 01:00:44.914
But Becky understood.

01:00:44.974 --> 01:00:47.754
Tom?

01:00:47.814 --> 01:00:50.504
Yes, Becky.

01:00:50.564 --> 01:00:54.836
Are they going to come and look for us?

01:00:54.896 --> 01:00:57.216
Of course!

01:00:57.276 --> 01:01:01.186
When the boat gets to St. Petersburg?

01:01:01.246 --> 01:01:04.454
But how can they find us?

01:01:04.514 --> 01:01:07.942
in these hundreds of tunnels.

01:01:08.002 --> 01:01:10.202
Oh, Tom!

01:01:10.263 --> 01:01:12.004
Tom!

01:01:12.064 --> 01:01:17.086
We're going to die in here!

01:01:17.146 --> 01:01:22.108
Becky began to cry again.

01:01:22.168 --> 01:01:30.338
Then the candle went out, and the two children were in the dark.

01:01:30.398 --> 01:01:35.824
They sat for hours and hours.

01:01:35.884 --> 01:01:43.346
They slept a little, then woke up, then slept again.

01:01:43.406 --> 01:01:49.947
Was it Sunday now or Monday?

01:01:50.007 --> 01:01:54.478
Suddenly Tom sat up.

01:01:54.538 --> 01:02:00.168
Listen, somebody's calling.

01:02:00.228 --> 01:02:05.257
The two children listened.

01:02:05.318 --> 01:02:10.388
They heard it again, a little nearer.

01:02:10.448 --> 01:02:13.560
They called back.

01:02:13.620 --> 01:02:21.472
Then they began to walk down the tunnel in the dark, with their hands on the wall.

01:02:21.533 --> 01:02:25.634
They stopped and listened again.

01:02:25.694 --> 01:02:30.118
But now they couldn't hear anything.

01:02:30.178 --> 01:02:36.103
Slowly, they went back to their river.

01:02:36.163 --> 01:02:43.874
They slept again and woke up very, very hungry.

01:02:43.935 --> 01:02:49.896
Perhaps it's Tuesday now, Tom thought.

01:02:49.956 --> 01:02:51.817
What can I do?

01:02:51.837 --> 01:02:55.878
I must do something.

01:02:55.938 --> 01:02:59.930
Then he had an idea.

01:02:59.990 --> 01:03:08.977
Becky, listen, I've got a long string in my pocket.

01:03:09.037 --> 01:03:16.142
I can go down some of the small tunnels and get back to you with the string.

01:03:16.202 --> 01:03:19.304
You wait here.

01:03:19.364 --> 01:03:29.084
Slowly and carefully, Tom went down the first tunnel on his hands and knees.

01:03:29.144 --> 01:03:36.272
Then the tunnel wall on his right finished, and there was nothing.

01:03:36.332 --> 01:03:53.886
Tom put out his hand to feel the floor, and just then, away to his right, he saw a hand, a hand with a candle.

01:03:53.946 --> 01:04:03.134
At once Tom called out, He cried.

01:04:03.194 --> 01:04:11.160
The hand moved, and Tom saw an arm and a face.

01:04:11.220 --> 01:04:15.504
It was engine Joe.

01:04:15.564 --> 01:04:27.742
Tom was very afraid, but engine Joe was afraid too, and he quickly ran away down the tunnel.

01:04:27.803 --> 01:04:31.714
Tom went back to Becky.

01:04:31.774 --> 01:04:36.114
but he did not tell her about engine Joe.

01:04:36.174 --> 01:04:48.136
Tom waited for an hour, then went into a different tunnel with his string, then a third tunnel.

01:04:48.196 --> 01:04:55.699
It was Tuesday evening and St. Petersburg waited.

01:04:55.759 --> 01:05:04.967
Many of the villagers were in the cave and they looked for the children day and night.

01:05:05.027 --> 01:05:13.314
But they heard nothing, saw nothing, and found nothing.

01:05:13.374 --> 01:05:20.419
Then, late that evening, there was a sudden noise in the streets.

01:05:20.479 --> 01:05:25.333
People began to run to the Thatcher's house.

01:05:25.393 --> 01:05:27.735
They're here!

01:05:27.795 --> 01:05:31.668
Vicki and Tom are here!

01:05:31.728 --> 01:05:38.221
Most of the village came to listen to Tom's story.

01:05:38.281 --> 01:05:43.612
It was in the sixth tunnel, he told them.

01:05:43.672 --> 01:05:51.153
I went to the end of my string and suddenly I could see daylight.

01:05:51.213 --> 01:05:55.514
There was a little hole in the cave wall.

01:05:55.574 --> 01:06:01.967
I put my head out and there was the river.

01:06:02.028 --> 01:06:05.643
right under my nose.

01:06:05.703 --> 01:06:13.279
I went back and got Becky and we climbed out through the hole.

01:06:13.339 --> 01:06:17.733
Then we stopped a boat on the river.

01:06:17.793 --> 01:06:25.978
We were five miles from the mouth of the cave.

01:06:26.038 --> 01:06:39.990
Tom was very tired after his three days in the cave, and he went to bed and stayed there for two days.

01:06:40.051 --> 01:06:49.302
He heard about Huck and went to see him on Sunday, and then every day.

01:06:49.362 --> 01:06:54.734
But Mrs. Douglas was always in the room.

01:06:54.794 --> 01:06:58.516
You can just say hello.

01:06:58.576 --> 01:07:03.779
She told Tom, and then you must go.

01:07:03.839 --> 01:07:11.422
Hock is very ill, and he needs to sleep.

01:07:11.482 --> 01:07:23.167
So Tom could not talk about anything exciting, and he could not tell Hock about engine Joe.

01:07:23.227 --> 01:07:34.492
One day, about two weeks after the picnic, Tom was in Becky's house, and her father came in.

01:07:34.552 --> 01:07:39.936
Well, Tom, Mr. Thatcher said.

01:07:39.996 --> 01:07:46.430
Would you like to go back to the cave again, one day?

01:07:46.490 --> 01:07:52.494
I'm not afraid of that cave, said Tom.

01:07:52.554 --> 01:07:55.998
Mr. Thatcher laughed.

01:07:56.058 --> 01:08:01.062
There are a lot of people like you, Tom.

01:08:01.122 --> 01:08:06.334
But nobody's going into that cave again.

01:08:06.395 --> 01:08:12.226
There are big doors across the cave mouth now.

01:08:12.286 --> 01:08:16.757
And nobody can open them.

01:08:16.818 --> 01:08:21.430
Tom's face went white.

01:08:21.489 --> 01:08:37.547
But Mr. Thatcher, An hour later, fifty men were at the cave, and they opened the doors.

01:08:37.606 --> 01:08:53.070
Engine Joe was on the ground, dead, his face to the door, and his knife in his hand.

01:08:53.130 --> 01:09:00.804
under the cross.

01:09:00.865 --> 01:09:08.870
The day after engine Joe's funeral, Hock was out of bed.

01:09:08.930 --> 01:09:14.553
He and Tom walked slowly out of the village.

01:09:14.613 --> 01:09:27.235
They had a good long talk, and Hock heard all about the picnic, the cave, and engine Joe.

01:09:27.294 --> 01:09:34.312
We're never gonna find the money now, said Huck.

01:09:34.372 --> 01:09:36.252
Huck?

01:09:36.312 --> 01:09:38.213
Said Tom.

01:09:38.273 --> 01:09:42.284
The money isn't in St. Petersburg.

01:09:42.344 --> 01:09:44.976
It's in the cave.

01:09:45.036 --> 01:09:47.716
I know it is.

01:09:47.776 --> 01:09:52.378
Why was engine Joe in the cave?

01:09:52.438 --> 01:09:59.776
Because he took the box of money there, right?

01:09:59.836 --> 01:10:03.992
Huck looked excited.

01:10:04.052 --> 01:10:08.565
Say that again, Tom.

01:10:08.625 --> 01:10:13.678
The money's in the cave.

01:10:13.738 --> 01:10:17.540
And we can get to it easily.

01:10:17.600 --> 01:10:20.452
Let's go there now.

01:10:20.512 --> 01:10:25.476
I've got some candles and a long string.

01:10:25.536 --> 01:10:31.622
We can take a boat and put it back later.

01:10:31.682 --> 01:10:39.330
Twenty minutes later, the boys were in a boat on the Mississippi.

01:10:39.390 --> 01:10:48.567
They went eight miles down the river, and then Tom stopped by some small trees.

01:10:48.627 --> 01:10:50.998
Here we are!

01:10:51.058 --> 01:10:53.130
He said.

01:10:53.190 --> 01:10:58.254
Tom's hole was just behind the trees.

01:10:58.314 --> 01:11:02.864
Tom took a candle and climbed in.

01:11:02.924 --> 01:11:07.496
Huck climbed in after him.

01:11:07.556 --> 01:11:15.272
Engine Joe never found this hole, said Tom.

01:11:15.332 --> 01:11:20.857
Or he did find it and couldn't get through it.

01:11:20.917 --> 01:11:24.930
It's very small.

01:11:24.990 --> 01:11:31.835
The boys went carefully through the tunnels with their string.

01:11:31.895 --> 01:11:35.826
Then Tom stopped.

01:11:35.886 --> 01:11:40.258
I saw engine Joe about here.

01:11:40.318 --> 01:11:42.528
He said.

01:11:42.588 --> 01:11:44.939
And look, Huck.

01:11:45.000 --> 01:11:48.181
There's the cross.

01:11:48.241 --> 01:11:54.134
There is a big smoke cross on the tunnel wall.

01:11:54.194 --> 01:11:58.666
The boys looked up and down the tunnel.

01:11:58.726 --> 01:12:03.188
But there was no box of money.

01:12:03.248 --> 01:12:10.946
Engine Joe said, under the cross, said Tom.

01:12:11.006 --> 01:12:15.439
Perhaps it's under the ground.

01:12:15.499 --> 01:12:20.874
Look, we can move these stones.

01:12:20.934 --> 01:12:28.732
The boys took their knives and began to dig by the tunnel wall.

01:12:28.792 --> 01:12:36.650
Very soon they found a second smaller tunnel under the wall.

01:12:36.710 --> 01:12:44.387
They climbed down into it and came into a small room.

01:12:44.447 --> 01:12:58.234
There was a bed, two whiskey bottles, some old shoes, and the box of money.

01:12:58.294 --> 01:13:08.106
When somebody finds treasure, everybody hears about it very quickly.

01:13:08.166 --> 01:13:13.518
The two boys carry the box through the village.

01:13:13.578 --> 01:13:20.680
And when they got to Aunt Polly's house, half the village was with them.

01:13:20.740 --> 01:13:25.563
Everybody went into the house.

01:13:25.623 --> 01:13:28.564
Oh, Tom!

01:13:28.624 --> 01:13:29.970
Tom!

01:13:30.030 --> 01:13:32.666
cried Aunt Polly.

01:13:32.726 --> 01:13:36.058
What is it now?

01:13:36.118 --> 01:13:40.510
And what have you got there?

01:13:40.570 --> 01:13:47.412
Tom put the box on the table and opened it.

01:13:47.472 --> 01:13:53.464
There were $12,000 in that box.

01:13:53.524 --> 01:14:06.012
and suddenly Tom Sawyer and Huckleberry Finn were the richest people in St. Petersburg.

